.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt ZFS-SET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zfs-set
.Nd terminal UI and CLI for ZFS dataset properties
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl list
.Op Fl local
.Op Fl json
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl get Ar property Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl json
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl set Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl set Ar ...
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl inherit Ar property
.Op Fl inherit Ar ...
.Op Fl S
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl tree Ar property
.Op Fl json
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl where Ar property
.Op Fl json
.Nm
.Fl dump
.Op Fl r
.Op Ar dataset
.Nm
.Fl restore Ar file
.Op Fl n | Fl y | Fl check
.Nm
.Fl catalogue
.Op Fl json
.Nm
.Fl describe Ar property
.Op Fl json
.Nm
.Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a front-end for
.Xr zfs-get 8 ,
.Xr zfs-set 8
and
.Xr zfs-inherit 8 :
it shows every property of a dataset with its value and where the value comes
from, explains each one, lets you change them through a list of the allowed
values or a validated text field, and turns the edits into the exact
.Ql zfs set
and
.Ql zfs inherit
commands, shown for review before they run.
Pre-flight checks point out what zfs will refuse (a quota below the used
space, a volsize that is not a multiple of volblocksize, a pool feature not
enabled, a property the dataset type does not have) and what the change
implies (a mount point change unmounts and remounts, canmount=off unmounts
now, compression and checksum only affect new data, sync=disabled is unsafe,
Linux-only properties do nothing on
.Fx ) .
.Pp
Without options
.Nm
starts the interactive editor on
.Ar dataset ;
without a dataset it first shows a picker of every file system and volume,
with the dataset of the current directory preselected.
The options below are the non-interactive modes, for scripts and
configuration management; there
.Ar dataset
defaults to the one the current directory is on.
.Ss Model
Every property has a value and a source:
.Bl -tag -width "inherited from X" -compact
.It Sy local
set on the dataset itself with
.Ql zfs set ;
.It Sy received
set by
.Ql zfs receive ;
a later
.Ql zfs set
makes the source local but keeps the received value around, and
.Ql zfs inherit -S
reverts to it;
.It Sy inherited from X
the nearest ancestor that sets it;
.It Sy default
nobody sets it;
.It Sy temporary
a mount option overrides it until the next remount;
.It Sy -
a statistic, or not applicable.
.El
.Pp
Properties are inherited down the dataset tree when they are inheritable;
the others
.Po quota, reservation, canmount, the limits, volsize …
.Pc
apply only where they are set.
.Ql zfs inherit
refuses to clear those:
.Nm
resets them with
.Ql zfs inherit -S ,
which goes back to the received value if there is one and otherwise to the
default.
.Pp
Read-only statistics and the properties fixed at creation
.Po casesensitivity, normalization, utf8only, encryption, keyformat,
pbkdf2iters, volblocksize
.Pc
are listed but cannot be edited.
Per-key properties
.Po Ar userquota@USER , groupquota@GROUP , projectquota@ID
and the object-count variants
.Pc
are not in
.Ql zfs get all :
add them with
.Ic a
interactively, or name them with
.Fl get
and
.Fl set .
.Ss Interactive keys
.Bl -tag -width "ctrl+s, F10" -compact
.It Ic enter , e
edit the property: set a value, inherit, or revert to the received value
.It Ic i
inherit: clear the value set here
.Pq pending
.It Ic S
revert to the received value
.Pq pending, Ql zfs inherit -S
.It Ic a
add a user property
.Pq Ar module:name
or a per-key one
.Pq Ar userquota@NAME …
.It Ic d
drop the pending edit of the property
.It Ic A
apply: show the commands and the pre-flight notes, then run them
.It Ic u , r
undo the last edit; reload from the kernel
.It Ic t
the property up and down the tree: its value on every ancestor and on every
descendant that overrides it
.It Ic /
filter by name or description
.It Ic l
only the properties set on this dataset
.It Ic x
show the properties that do nothing on
.Fx
.It Ic D
switch dataset
.It Ic q , esc
back to the dataset list when the session started there, otherwise quit
.It Ic ? , h
help, key list
.El
.Pp
In the editor
.Ic ↑/↓
move between the action, the values, the options and the buttons,
.Ic space
selects or toggles,
.Ic enter
on a value selects it and confirms, on the text field confirms,
.Ic ctrl+s
confirms and
.Ic esc
cancels.
Long value lists
.Pq compression
open a filterable picker.
The options are
.Dq the children inherit it too
.Pq Ql zfs inherit -r Ar property No on each child
and, for mountpoint, sharenfs and sharesmb,
.Dq change the property only
.Pq Ql zfs set -u .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl list
Print every property of the dataset in catalogue order with its value, its
source and its meaning.
With
.Fl local
only the properties set on the dataset itself
.Pq local or received .
.It Fl get Ar property Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
Print the named properties with their source, received value and meaning.
Aliases
.Pq Ar compress , avail …
and per-key names
.Pq Ar userquota@bob
are accepted.
.It Fl set Ar property Ns = Ns Ar value
Set the property; may be repeated.
The value is validated against the catalogue before anything runs.
With
.Fl r
the children inherit the new value too
.Pq Ql zfs inherit -r Ar property No on each child, clearing what they had ;
with
.Fl u
mountpoint, sharenfs and sharesmb are changed without mounting or sharing
.Pq Ql zfs set -u .
.It Fl inherit Ar property
Clear the property on the dataset so it is inherited or reverts to the
default; may be repeated.
With
.Fl S
revert to the received value
.Pq Ql zfs inherit -S ;
with
.Fl r
on every descendant too
.Pq Ql zfs inherit -r .
.It Fl n
Print the
.Ql zfs
commands and the pre-flight notes without running them.
.It Fl y
Run the commands without asking.
.It Fl check
Dry run that exits 3 if anything would change and 0 if nothing would.
.It Fl tree Ar property
Show the property on every ancestor down to the dataset, and on every
descendant that sets it itself.
.It Fl where Ar property
List every file system and volume on the system that sets the property
itself, with the value.
.It Fl dump
Print a JSON snapshot of the properties the dataset sets itself
.Pq local and received ;
with
.Fl r
of every descendant too.
.It Fl restore Ar file
Bring every dataset recorded in a
.Fl dump
snapshot back to it: recorded values are set where they differ, values set
locally but not recorded are inherited.
Datasets that no longer exist are skipped with a warning.
.Fl n ,
.Fl y
and
.Fl check
apply.
.It Fl catalogue
Print every native property with its kind
.Pq settable, read-only, creation-only
and meaning, by group.
.It Fl describe Ar property
Print everything about one property: meaning, default, values with their
meaning, pool feature, whether it is inherited.
.It Fl json
JSON output for
.Fl list ,
.Fl get ,
.Fl tree ,
.Fl where ,
.Fl catalogue ,
.Fl describe
and
.Fl n .
.It Fl lenient
Accept property names that are not in the catalogue
.Pq a newer OpenZFS may know more .
.It Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on error
.Pq including a refused Ql zfs No command ;
2 when the confirmation was declined; 3 when
.Fl check
found pending changes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Preview the commands that switch a subtree to zstd, including the datasets
below that had their own compression setting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zfs-set -set compression=zstd -r -n tank/home
zfs set compression=zstd tank/home
zfs inherit -r compression tank/home/alice
zfs inherit -r compression tank/home/bob
note: compression affects only data written from now on; existing blocks keep the old lz4
.Ed
.Pp
Move a mount point without mounting anything yet, and see what it implies:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs-set -set mountpoint=/export/home -u -y tank/home
.Ed
.Pp
Keep the properties of a subtree under configuration management:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs-set -dump -r tank/home > props.json
# zfs-set -restore props.json -check || zfs-set -restore props.json -y
.Ed
.Pp
Which datasets set atime themselves, and what does sync=disabled mean:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ zfs-set -where atime
$ zfs-set -describe sync
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr facl 1 ,
.Xr zfs-allow 1 ,
.Xr zpool-set 1 ,
.Xr zfsprops 7 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zfs-inherit 8 ,
.Xr zfs-set 8
.Sh CAVEATS
.Ql zfs set
is not recursive; the
.Dq children inherit
option is
.Ql zfs inherit -r
on each child, which clears whatever they had set themselves.
.Pp
Changing
.Sy mountpoint
unmounts and remounts the file system and every child that inherits it; a
busy file system makes it fail.
.Sy canmount Ns =off
unmounts now,
.Sy readonly Ns =on
applies immediately to a mounted file system.
.Pp
.Sy sharesmb ,
the SELinux contexts,
.Sy nbmand ,
.Sy vscan ,
.Sy mlslabel
and
.Sy volthreading
do nothing on
.Fx ;
.Sy acltype Ns =posix
behaves as
.Sy off .
The catalogue follows OpenZFS 2.4; an unknown property is still shown and
can be set with
.Fl lenient .
